# A callable named at the walked root is called by an explicit CALL the translator emits
# (FABLE-OPUS-CODE-DATA-SPLIT-20260925-189 commit c4; D-03; callable priority -130): the walker calls
# nothing on its own (lmx_walk_is_callable goes with the `native` word).  A bare `ping` statement is
# the step CALL(ping) with its result dropped; `int: r ping` binds r to the CALL's result.  The exit
# code is r - 7: 0.
fn: ping () int
    return: 7
end: ping

ping
int: r ping
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: r - 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
